  "body": "GPU adapter selection on hybrid laptops, and a frame-stall log (#74, user-reported: Intel UHD + Quadro P3200 never renders / lags 1-2 s on an empty orbit).\n\n**What changed** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/`)\n- `gpu_init.rs` (new, out of `shell.rs`): within each backend group of the existing chain, enumerate every adapter and log one `gpu: seen ...` line each (name, vendor, device id, type, backend, surface-compatible). Try adapters one by one: device, surface config, configure - checked for errors, not assumed. A failure logs `gpu: \"<name>\" via <backend> failed: <reason> - trying the next adapter`; failed adapters aren't retried. If none works, the refusal lists every adapter tried and why, on stderr and in a native error dialog.\n- `gpu_select.rs` (+ tests, new): ordering and surface config as pure functions. Order: `--gpu <name>` / `CAMCRAFT_GPU` -> the HighPerformance pick -> every other surface-compatible adapter, discrete > integrated > virtual > other > software; ties to the native API (DX12 on Windows, Metal on macOS, Vulkan elsewhere); incompatible adapters skipped by name.\n- Surface config from the surface's reported capabilities (preferred format, Fifo unless missing, Opaque alpha if offered) instead of `get_default_config` + hard-coded AutoVsync.\n- `--gpu <part of name>` (beats `CAMCRAFT_GPU`), following `--gpu-backend`; no preferences page yet (no per-machine settings store) - recorded in RECOMMENDED.md.\n- `frame_watch.rs` (new): a frame over 100 ms logs one line with time per phase (commands+scene, ui, acquire, encode, submit+present), at most one line per 5 s.\n\n**Stall**: not reproduced headlessly - nothing on the idle frame path blocks (GPU readbacks are tests/diagnostics only). Leading suspect: Vulkan cross-adapter copy on Optimus; DX12-first should avoid it. Issue stays open for the reporter's log.\n\n**Tests**: `gpu_select::tests` (9: discrete_before_integrated_before_cpu, user_choice_wins_case_insensitively, unmatched_choice_is_said_and_auto_order_stands, high_performance_pick_leads_on_its_best_backend, unpresentable_adapters_are_skipped_by_name, nothing_to_order_is_empty_not_a_panic, log_line_names_every_field, config_comes_from_reported_capabilities, incompatible_surface_refuses_by_name), `frame_watch::tests` (3), `gpu::tests::adapter_choice_flag_then_env`. camcraft-ui lib 230 passed; gpu_render 9; shell 19; clippy -D warnings clean; quick gate green.\n\nChangelog: fix(ui): GPU startup tries adapters one by one (named choice, high-performance, discrete before integrated, native backend first), configures the surface from its reported capabilities, adds --gpu/CAMCRAFT_GPU, refuses by name listing every adapter tried, and logs frames over 100 ms by phase\n\nRefs #74\n",
